{"id":"CVE-2006-1987","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2006-04-21T22:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T17:35:30.729Z","description":"Apple Safari 2.0.3 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service and possibly execute code via an invalid FRAME tag, possibly due to (1) multiple SCROLLING attributes with no values, or (2) a SRC attribute with no value.  NOTE: due to lack of diagnosis by the researcher, it is unclear which vector is responsible.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://security-protocols.com/poc/sp-x26-4.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.security-protocols.com/sp-x26-advisory.php","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/25946","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"macosx-safari-dos(25946)"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2006/1452","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2006-1452"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/17634","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"17634"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/19686","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"19686"}],"vendors":["apple"]}
{"id":"CVE-2006-1988","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2006-04-21T22:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T17:35:31.288Z","description":"The WebTextRenderer(WebInternal) _CG_drawRun:style:geometry: function in Apple Safari 2.0.3 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (application crash) via an HTML LI tag with a large VALUE attribute (list item number), which triggers a null dereference in QPainter::drawText, probably due to a failed memory allocation that uses the VALUE.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.security-protocols.com/sp-x26-advisory.php","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/25946","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"macosx-safari-dos(25946)"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2006/1452","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2006-1452"},{"url":"http://security-protocols.com/poc/sp-x26-2.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/17634","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"17634"},{"url":"http://www.osvdb.org/24823","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_OSVDB"],"name":"24823"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/19686","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"19686"}],"vendors":["apple"]}
{"id":"CVE-2006-3224","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2006-06-26T16:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T18:23:20.886Z","description":"Apple Safari 2.0.3 (417.9.3) on Mac OS X 10.4.6 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (CPU consumption) via Javascript with an infinite for loop.  NOTE: it could be argued that this is not a vulnerability, unless it interferes with the operation of the system outside of the scope of Safari itself.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://lists.grok.org.uk/pipermail/full-disclosure/2006-May/046150.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_FULLDISC"],"name":"20060519 Apple Safari 2.0.3 (417.9.3) JavaScript - Denial of Service"},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/26558","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"safari-javascript-dos(26558)"}],"vendors":["apple"]}
{"id":"CVE-2006-3372","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2006-07-06T20:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T18:23:21.272Z","description":"Apple Safari 2.0.4/419.3 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (application crash) via a DHTML setAttributeNode function call with zero arguments, which triggers a null dereference.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://browserfun.blogspot.com/2006/07/mobb-5-dhtml-setattributenode.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/27594","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"safari-dhtml-setattributenode-dos(27594)"},{"url":"http://securitytracker.com/id?1016441","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1016441"},{"url":"http://www.osvdb.org/26838","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_OSVDB"],"name":"26838"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2006/2671","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2006-2671"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/18822","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"18822"}],"exploitdb":[{"edb":"28165","title":"Apple Safari Web Browser 2.0.4 - DHTML SetAttributeNode() Null Dereference Denial of Service","type":"dos","platform":"osx","date":"2006-07-05","verified":"1"}],"vendors":["apple"]}
{"id":"CVE-2006-3946","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2006-07-31T23:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T18:48:39.402Z","description":"WebCore in Apple Mac OS X 10.3.9 and 10.4 through 10.4.7 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (crash) and possibly execute arbitrary code via crafted HTML that triggers a \"memory management error\" in WebKit, possibly due to a buffer overflow, as originally reported for the KHTMLParser::popOneBlock function in Apple Safari 2.0.4 using Javascript that changes document.body.innerHTML within a DIV tag.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://browserfun.blogspot.com/2006/07/mobb-31-safari-khtmlparserpoponeblock.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/28081","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"safari-khtmlparser-code-execution(28081)"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/22187","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"22187"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2006/3852","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2006-3852"},{"url":"http://www.osvdb.org/27534","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_OSVDB"],"name":"27534"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/21271","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"21271"},{"url":"http://lists.apple.com/archives/security-announce/2006/Sep/msg00002.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_APPLE"],"name":"APPLE-SA-2006-09-29"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/19250","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"19250"},{"url":"http://securitytracker.com/id?1016957","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1016957"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2006/3069","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2006-3069"}],"vendors":["apple"]}
{"id":"CVE-2006-6238","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2006-12-03T18:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T20:02:43.458Z","description":"The AutoFill feature in Apple Safari 2.0.4 does not properly verify that all automatically populated form fields are visible to the user, which allows remote attackers to obtain sensitive information, such as usernames and passwords, via input fields of zero width, a variant of CVE-2006-6077.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://tearesolutions.com/2006/11/how_to_steal_passwords_from_safaris_autofill.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/23066","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"23066"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/21329","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"21329"}],"vendors":["apple"]}
